\begin_inset Formula $x$
\end_inset

 satisfies the Uncompensated Law of Demand.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Proof

\bar under
Part F.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Proof
\begin_inset space \quad{}
\end_inset

A demand function 
\begin_inset Formula $x$
\end_inset

 satisfies the Uncompensated Law of Demand iff 
\begin_inset Formula $\forall\ \{p,p^{\prime}\}\subseteq\mathbb{R}_{++}^{L}$
\end_inset

, 
\begin_inset Formula $\forall\ w\in\mathbb{R}_{+}$
\end_inset

,
\begin_inset Formula 
\[
(p^{\prime}-p)\cdot\left(x(p^{\prime},w)-x(p,w)\right)\leq0
\]

\end_inset

with strict inequality when 
